 "observations": [
  "The title page is set in Roman capitals, with three lines in black letter (Fraktur), transcribed in Roman type: «Herausgegeben» (L05), «Mit fünf Tafeln in Lichtdruck» (L11) and «Otto Harrassowitz · Leipzig» (L13). The transliterated names keep the diacritics of the print: the dots below Ṣ, Ḍ and Ḥ, the macrons, the haček of Ǧ and the breve below Ḫ of «AL-ḪUWĀRIZMĪ», the half ring of «ǦAʿFAR». The shelfmark of the manuscript, «COD. 4247», stands between two thin slanting strokes, transcribed as slashes; its figures are old-style. A rule separates the date, «MCMXXVI», 1926, from the publisher's line.",
  "L10: the editor's name is printed «MŹIK», with an acute accent over the Z, where the series title page prints «MŽIK», with a haček (frame 212, L04), the form of the name Mžik; see the critical note. The reprint's copy of this page has the same accent (frame 214).",
  "The volume is the third of the series «Bibliothek arabischer Historiker und Geographen» (frame 212). Its back, frame 209, carries the imprint."
